meta {
  name: 08 - Get Whole Document Tree
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/blocks?id={{document_id}}&maxDepth=-1&fetchMetadata=false
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  id: {{document_id}}
  maxDepth: -1
  fetchMetadata: false
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{craft_token}}
}

docs {
  Tests whether one call on the document root (not a single company) with
  maxDepth=-1 returns all 76 companies AND their nested content (task
  blocks included) in one response - confirmed for a single company by
  request 06 (collectionItem -> content: [h2, richUrl, task, task, ...]).

  If this works, fetch_new_offers() can walk this single tree instead of
  76 separate calls: for each collectionItem in the collection's content,
  scan its content list for text blocks with taskInfo.state == "todo",
  and pair each with the nearest preceding richUrl block (same content
  list) for the offer link.

  Response may be large (76 companies x a handful of blocks each) - if it
  gets unwieldy to paste back, just report the item count and whether the
  nesting looks like request 06's shape, rather than the full JSON.

  Read-only, safe to run freely.
}
